hat was probably inspired by Robert E. Howard novels and embraced a serpent motif that very arguably has no purpose being conflated with the god Set. You know them, you love them. They made religion dark and cool before the Sabbat was a glimmer in your sire\u2019s eye.<br /> <br /> The Settites have long since been established as a vast network of sometimes only vaguely related cults and theological concepts. While the Theophidian Orthodoxy is the one we\u2019re most familiar with - you know, the Set as Gnosticism folks - there have always been others established and dozens, if not hundred, of others implied to exist.<br /> <br /> Heck, part of revised\u2019s settite metaplot was the plot hook that a Settite methuselah awoke to create a cult dedicated to the elimination of unorthodox cults and that the current circumstance of settite religions in play would probably follow chronicles that showcased the struggle between disparate settite cults and beliefs, while many cults turned against the Theophidians, and the Theophidians hoped to clean house for the Time of Judgement and the return of Set.<br /> <br /> As we all know, that no longer happened.<br /> <br /> So in V5, the Followers of Set have rebranded as the Ministry and are seeking to align themselves with the Anarch Movement, newly splintered away in full from the Camarilla and now a truly independent sect. <br /> <br /> It was thinking about all of these things and how I\u2019ve always felt that more emphasis could be placed upon the diversity of Settite cults, that led me to this though.<br /> <br /> FUTURE FATES<br /> \u2022Ministry, never heard of her (V20)<br /> -This is V20 and all prior editions<br /> <br /> \u2022Check the new hotness (V5)<br /> -This is the V5 canon<br /> <br /> (Future Fates generally presents three options: 0%, 100%, and somewhere in between - I\u2019m now going into the third option)<br /> <br /> \u2022Have You Heard The Good Word? (V20.5)<br /> -Historically, the Settites have suffered from the distrust of both the Camarilla and Anarchs. The Sabbat didn\u2019t distrust them - they hated them. So, for the clan, the game was to figure out ways to lure individual, desperate members of these secular sects towards them for aid. Surely, there had to be a better way.<br /> <br /> Both the Camarilla and Anarch Movement are nominally secular, despite the elders cults of the former and the religious movement of the latter. Both however, didn\u2019t trust what the Settites were pushing. The Camarilla couldn\u2019t openly work with those who preached of the antediluvians and the Anarchs learned from habit.<br /> <br /> How then to get close? Why, a variety of cult designed specifically for both sects of course. Enter the Ministry.<br /> <br /> The Ministry was polished, intellectual, and enlightened in the fashion of philosophical satanists. They built good will through advocacy of popular ideas - freedom amongst the Anarchs and stability amongst the Camarilla. They openly disdained the foolish superstitions of their primitive clan mates, explaining that blood gods were foolish myths unfit for modern unlife.<br /> <br /> They explained that they used Set simply as a symbol for a philosophical ideal - whether that ideal was Freedom From Tyranny or Control Over Self depended on who the Settite was selling themselves to. The Ministry openly mocked Noddism, posited modern theories, and worked diligently to always be palatable.<br /> <br /> The Ministry\u2019s greatest strength was the flexibility of its doctrine, which could be shifted to conform whatever community the settite entered. This was particularly accepted in America, where people were already familiar with the concept of dozens of different specific beliefs existing as distinct groups under a common banner. The Settites could present whatever face worked best, knowing that external doctrine was always malleable - the truth of Set was found within after all.<br /> <br /> The Ministry was not without controversy from without or from within but the attacks against it by both the Sabbat and its parent clan worked well to endear the new movement to the Camarilla and the Anarchs. It may be centuries until a Settite is on the Inner Circle of the Camarilla, but some domains began to welcome the philosophers, particularly given their willingness to combat the Sabbat and Noddism. Anarchs similarly opened their arms to those seeking freedom from oppression, including religious oppression, and amongst the shiftless masses of Anarchs and Autarkis the Ministry would find many potential converts.<br /> <br /> Was the Ministry a ploy to infiltrate the sects? Was it a genuine gathering of religious and philosophical movements, forced to flee the oppression and persecution of its parent clan? Was it an independent movement or a cover for a network of alliances between unorthodox settite groups?<br /> <br /> You, the ST, may decide. Whatever suits your game is the best answer and whatever you find the most interesting.<br /> <br /> Remember - Your Will is the Only Law.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im actually fascinated by the God Set, so I\u2019m kind of torn, fun fact that Set hated Apothis the giant snake In Egyptian Mythology that tries to swallow the sun every night. And was the only a god that was immune to his Hypnotic glare. You could do a interesting thing with that In your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T14:04:02-07:00","id":1408020,"title":"","content":"Aye, there\u2019s definitely a place somewhere for analysis of Set\u2019s relationship with Apophis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T14:20:38-07:00","id":1408024,"title":"","content":"<b>Alternate V5 Plots</b><br /> <br /> 1. <b>Noctis Invictus</b>: Hardelstadt is assassinated by Theo Bell but the reason is that it was done at the hands of Jan Pieterszoon as the two of them announce the creation of their own version of the Camarilla. They form a boardroom and suit version of the Anarchs as an alternative to rule by Princes and have made a Devil's alliance with Marcus Vitel. Many cities join into this economic and military alliance that presents a fourth alternative to the Anarchs/Camarilla/Sabbat trinity. Theo and Jan are put on the Red List as a result.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Lasombra Defection</b>: The Lasombra defection was organized by Lucita of Aragon as she discovers that the Sabbat is pretty much unsalvagable by the time of 2018. The defection is something that happens in large part because of the failed Gehenna Crusade, the rising of the Lasombra Antediluvian, and the Second Inquisiton. The Masquerade must be preserved and Lucita is forced to once more face her slow return to Humanity.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Operation: Daystar</b>: The Technocracy has abandoned its war against the Traditions because they have come to the conclusion they have been defeated. They since restructure themselves for the purposes of eliminating the other group of reality deviants in the world with the Camarilla. This is not because the Technocracy are concerned about all the humans that vampires have killed but the belief that them being &quot;outed&quot; by science is inevitable as well as the belief they will gain vast power from the removal of Kindred masters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T14:26:06-07:00","id":1408025,"title":"","content":"In my noddist theory/headcanon, Apophis was the original Antediluvian of the Setites. Diablerized by Set, who did an Augustus Giovanni on them. It explains a number of discrepancies, such as the Setite clan being much older than Set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T15:04:44-07:00","id":1408037,"title":"","content":"Those are cool ideas CTPhipps!<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve thought more about the Lasombra defection then I have the changes to the Camarilla, which I figured I\u2019d need to do some more sit down reading to truly appreciate the direction that V5 chose to go, but these are both interesting ideas!<br /> <br /> The idea of harnessing the sort of middle ground that\u2019s always existed between Camarilla orthodoxy and Anarchs as well as friendly independents such as Vancouver or Cairo has always been interesting to me and this idea definitely gives an opportunity for that sort of thing. I\u2019m tempted to call this something like \u2018The Silicon Tower\u2019 option, the Camarilla revamped for the 21st century through compromise with the Anarchs - similar to the Camarilla\u2019s creation in a way.<br /> <br /> (I\u2019ve also mulled over the idea of replacing Theo Bell with Tyler for the Hardestalt plot if I used it - the Camarilla-Anarch War is a bit more then I usually want, but it\u2019s definitely an interesting option imo; but again I need to sit down with the lore more)<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve thought a lot more about the Lasombra defection, so I can\u2019t believe that tying in Lucita never occurred to me XD. Generally I used the Gehenna Crusade/Fourth Sabbat Civil War as an inciting incident for the defection, alongside personal ambition and rumors of the Founder - but I usually used Giangaleazzo and his defection and delivery of Milan to the Ivory Tower as the catalyst of many Ministers jumping ship. Lucita though is definitely an interesting angle.<br /> <br /> As far as the Technocracy, I\u2019ll admit I hadn\u2019t been thinking about them much - both to focus on Vampire and because we don\u2019t have much solid for M5 yet - but I can certainly see something like a \u2018Project: Daystar\u2019 existing within the Technocratic Union, even without the fallout of a Technocratic Civil War.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d never thought about that for Set Trollroot, but it is an interesting idea. I usually, for general WoD games that aren\u2019t focusing on the Settites, go with him being embraced by a wanderer of the second generation (who may also be Ravnos\u2019 and/or Osiris\u2019 sire) with Apophis being a spiritual being who Set has a complex relationship with, both harnessing the being\u2019s power for gain but also planning to betray it and become the true master (or \u2018Demiurge\u2019 if you will...); but that\u2019s definitely also an interesting route.<br /> <br /> Thanks to the folks who chose to post, definitely interesting stuff and I hope we get a lot of ideas flowing in here!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T15:11:45-07:00","id":1408039,"title":"","content":"the sabbat still has it share of cunning members,they are intelligent and can pass for human. but make no mistake,they have as much iin common as with human as a balck hole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T15:25:05-07:00","id":1408043,"title":"","content":"I really hope they confirm Lucita in the Camarilla in the next supplement,<br /> otherwise, we'll have to suffer through Phipps crying over his waifu for yet another decade or so","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T15:37:48-07:00","id":1408048,"title":"","content":"I mean, sure Nicolas - fair enough, I guess I\u2019m just confused what that has to do with this specifically.<br /> <br /> Also Pleiades, I don\u2019t know if you and CTPhipps are friends and that\u2019s just how you razz one another - if so, I get that and my bad for saying this - but that\u2019s kinda rude and I\u2019d prefer if you didn\u2019t talk about other posters like that in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T16:01:25-07:00","id":1408057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408006-v20-5-best-of-both-headcanon-thread?p=1408048#post1408048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, sure Nicolas - fair enough, I guess I\u2019m just confused what that has to do with this specifically.<br /> <br /> Also Pleiades, I don\u2019t know if you and CTPhipps are friends and that\u2019s just how you razz one another - if so, I get that and my bad for saying this - but that\u2019s kinda rude and I\u2019d prefer if you didn\u2019t talk about other posters like that in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fine, I've asked several questions related to Lucita in media and often make fun of myself regarding being her fanboy.<br /> <br /> Hilariously, Dixie from Onyx Path had the same bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-13-2020, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T16:14:57-07:00","id":1408061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408006-v20-5-best-of-both-headcanon-thread?p=1408018#post1408018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Im actually fascinated by the God Set, so I\u2019m kind of torn, fun fact that Set hated Apothis the giant snake In Egyptian Mythology that tries to swallow the sun every night. And was the only a god that was immune to his Hypnotic glare. You could do a interesting thing with that In your game.</div> </div> </div> </div>My own personal take has been that any connection between Set (or rather, the vampire cult that worships him) and Apep/Apophis is entirely that of werewolves trying to fit parts of human mythology into their own cosmology (much in the way they consider Fenris a hero and Odin and the other Aesir villains).<br /> <br /> The Set of Vampire, meanwhile, is/was the Lord of the Red Desert, a creature of unrestrained aggression and instinct, a living storm who stands in stark contrast to his much more balanced and restrained brother Osiris, the Lord of the Black Soil, and the other god-like Antediluvian (in the pre-Flood sense, not the ancient vampire sense) beings of Heliopolis. He is loyal to Ra (the Sun) and fights for him, but at some point, he turns against his brother and murders him. At this point, he's an outcast and at war with the rest of his family, and it's during this time that he becomes a vampire. (Again, this is my own personal take.) If you're a Noddist, this is when he meets Cain(e) (I ignore the second generation), but parts of his Set's cult believe that he became a vampire on his own, either doing something in the underworld or as a result of killing his brother. But at this point, he's fully a creature of Isfet, the counterpart to Ma'at (and neither concept/force can exist without the other).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T20:49:30-07:00","id":1408097,"title":"","content":"I had assumed that the Ministry were the insufficiently orthodox Setites who needed refuge from the hardcore fundamentalist elders - not that they would ever tip their hand and show their vulnerability to their new allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T21:38:28-07:00","id":1408099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408006-v20-5-best-of-both-headcanon-thread?p=1408048#post1408048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, sure Nicolas - fair enough, I guess I\u2019m just confused what that has to do with this specifically.<br /> <br /> Also Pleiades, I don\u2019t know if you and CTPhipps are friends and that\u2019s just how you razz one another - if so, I get that and my bad for saying this - but that\u2019s kinda rude and I\u2019d prefer if you didn\u2019t talk about other posters like that in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies,i think i posted in the wrong thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T05:28:13-07:00","id":1408130,"title":"","content":"<br /> The Camarilla elders are behind the SI, the Sabbat elders fabricated the Gehenna war and are killing their childer in cargo crates; The Elders of both sects have largely gotten along over the years and enjoy throwing neonates at eachother. They've realised that the population of neonates is too high and they're getting too rebelious and they need a cull and a reminder of why they serve. The Sabbat actually have set up a Methuselah in the middle east to take some blame.<br /> <br /> The V5 Tremere split was self inflicted, and is really just an attempt to move away from the perception that they're monopolistic monsters and move towards the illusion of a vibrant market with competitors. Ironically, it helps them crush competitors; it gives them a great chance to put chantries into cities that never in their right mind would allow Tremere to set up shop, and those chantries try to fight the wonderful wave of<i> Rites of the Blood</i> Anarch sorceries and the Assamite influx. <br /> <br /> V5 thinbloods: Doesn't happen. Save it for a Gehenna scenario.<br /> V5 clan weaknesses and disciplines: Doesn't happen, save it for a Gehenna scenario.<br /> <br /> Hecata: So they kill the elder Giovanni, they muse about creating a guild called the hecata, which lasts for a short amount of time before the necromancers split and go their separate ways as bloodlines. Best possible outcome for necromancers I think.<br /> <br /> Lasombra defection; Exaggerated. I really, really like lasombra, and would like to see them in the Camarilla, but the way it's done and the scale of it in V5 doesn't work with the reality of the setting. I do think more Sabbat elders are joining the Camarilla out of fears their plans to cull the neonates will blow up in their face (of course, the elders that stay loyal will point to the defectors as the ones guilty of betraying them)<br /> <br /> The Ministry: this one's a tough one.<br /> I think infiltrating the anarchs is a great idea. The name &quot;The ministry&quot; is fucking rediculous and needs to go. Works as a nickname and no more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-14-2020, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T06:01:40-07:00","id":1408137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408006-v20-5-best-of-both-headcanon-thread?p=1408061#post1408061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My own personal take has been that any connection between Set (or rather, the vampire cult that worships him) and Apep/Apophis is entirely that of werewolves trying to fit parts of human mythology into their own cosmology (much in the way they consider Fenris a hero and Odin and the other Aesir villains).<br /> <br /> The Set of Vampire, meanwhile, is/was the Lord of the Red Desert, a creature of unrestrained aggression and instinct, a living storm who stands in stark contrast to his much more balanced and restrained brother Osiris, the Lord of the Black Soil, and the other god-like Antediluvian (in the pre-Flood sense, not the ancient vampire sense) beings of Heliopolis. He is loyal to Ra (the Sun) and fights for him, but at some point, he turns against his brother and murders him. At this point, he's an outcast and at war with the rest of his family, and it's during this time that he becomes a vampire. (Again, this is my own personal take.) If you're a Noddist, this is when he meets Cain(e) (I ignore the second generation), but parts of his Set's cult believe that he became a vampire on his own, either doing something in the underworld or as a result of killing his brother. But at this point, he's fully a creature of Isfet, the counterpart to Ma'at (and neither concept/force can exist without the other).</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems less interesting, then a story of a God that was Demonized because of his Association With foreigners and thus foreign Conquers, to be more interesting then White Wolfs crappy version,<br /> <br /> That\u2019s a common thing in Speculative fiction about old mythology , they have a surface level view of things, and their for change thing to make it \u201cbetter\u201d with out understanding the Cultural And Historical Context,<br /> <br /> For a example portraying Zeus as rapist is a surface level Observation That ignores the context of him as The Hellas God of \u201c civilization\u201d and Hellas law, the ancient Hellaians (and certain people today) believes themselves to be the greatest culture ever! And Athens was known for being very misogynistic even by the standards of the Ancient Wolrd.<br /> <br /> So you could do something about how Zeus\u2019s rape of women represents the Patriarchal feeling common in most so called Civilizations and how it continued in similar societies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T07:32:18-07:00","id":1408150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408006-v20-5-best-of-both-headcanon-thread?p=1408048#post1408048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Pleiades, I don\u2019t know if you and CTPhipps are friends and that\u2019s just how you razz one another - if so, I get that and my bad for saying this - but that\u2019s kinda rude and I\u2019d prefer if you didn\u2019t talk about other posters like that in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like memeing with Phipps<br /> <br /> however, this forum lacks proper emojis,<br /> as a result, such posts tend to sound hostile","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T07:56:42-07:00","id":1408153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408006-v20-5-best-of-both-headcanon-thread?p=1408043#post1408043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hope they confirm Lucita in the Camarilla in the next supplement,<br /> otherwise, we'll have to suffer through Phipps crying over his waifu for yet another decade or so</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Heh, I hope to see her in ANY supplement. My favorite character from my favorite clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T08:21:09-07:00","id":1408161,"title":"","content":"Crazy headcannon: Set <i>is </i>Caine. Apophis/Apep is the &quot;angel&quot; that changed him. Osiris is the murdered brother abel and Horus is the Seth that challenged him. Caine hates god. Set hates god. The other Antes are Ra's servants who fuck with Set, the Antes are the unworthy grandchilder of Caine....<br /> <br /> Yeah it could use some fleshing out. But I like that the Settites believe in a clusterfuck of origin stories due to the chinese-whispers game of lies they all pull.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T08:38:16-07:00","id":1408169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408006-v20-5-best-of-both-headcanon-thread?p=1408037#post1408037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d never thought about that for Set Trollroot, but it is an interesting idea. I usually, for general WoD games that aren\u2019t focusing on the Settites, go with him being embraced by a wanderer of the second generation (who may also be Ravnos\u2019 and/or Osiris\u2019 sire) with Apophis being a spiritual being who Set has a complex relationship with, both harnessing the being\u2019s power for gain but also planning to betray it and become the true master (or \u2018Demiurge\u2019 if you will...); but that\u2019s definitely also an interesting route.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back in the day, before the board deluge if you will, it was noted that Set as a living man and famed warrior went into the western desert of Egypt. One of the most hostile terrains on Earth. He came back a vampire with animal features. The most diverged and probably oldest of his lines do not have Serpentis, they have Protean. It spelled Gangrel to most. Ennoia was also active and embracing in the middle east around this time.<br /> <br /> Osiris sire... well we can say with some confidence who she was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408006-v20-5-best-of-both-headcanon-thread?p=1408061#post1408061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My own personal take has been that any connection between Set (or rather, the vampire cult that worships him) and Apep/Apophis is entirely that of werewolves trying to fit parts of human mythology into their own cosmology (much in the way they consider Fenris a hero and Odin and the other Aesir villains).<br /> <br /> The Set of Vampire, meanwhile, is/was the Lord of the Red Desert, a creature of unrestrained aggression and instinct, a living storm who stands in stark contrast to his much more balanced and restrained brother Osiris, the Lord of the Black Soil, and the other god-like Antediluvian (in the pre-Flood sense, not the ancient vampire sense) beings of Heliopolis. He is loyal to Ra (the Sun) and fights for him, but at some point, he turns against his brother and murders him. At this point, he's an outcast and at war with the rest of his family, and it's during this time that he becomes a vampire. (Again, this is my own personal take.) If you're a Noddist, this is when he meets Cain(e) (I ignore the second generation), but parts of his Set's cult believe that he became a vampire on his own, either doing something in the underworld or as a result of killing his brother. But at this point, he's fully a creature of Isfet, the counterpart to Ma'at (and neither concept/force can exist without the other).</div> </div> </div> </div>It is an interesting viewpoint, Mr. Howard. Set as a wight. But Set is the Antediluvian we know them most about, more I think than even Tremere and Augustus Giovanni. I shall make a thread on it soon I think.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T09:25:03-07:00","id":1408175,"title":"","content":"Really there's no reason you can't take the entire metaplot out of V5 and use it with the V20 mechanics.<br /> <br /> Since I've run games in pre-Christian settings, my personal head canon is that only a handful of clans at most are truly descended from Caine, they just share a similiar curse. The whole Caine and the first city myth only became popular in the middle ages with a lot of the elders either dying, choosing to go into Torpor, or in other cases like Michael and Cappadocius, converted to Christianity and had a vested interest in going along with the myth to support their relatively new faith. The god that would become Shiva/Dionysus was the Malkavian origin. Set really was a &quot;god&quot; in Egypt and the first or maybe second vampire in that line. The Gangrel myth about Ennoia the beast goddess and Churka the night god is actually accurate for the Gangrel origin. The Ravnos were created to combat demons they were made to resemble (other vampires or Wan Kuei). The Toreador really are the descendants of Ishtar and Gangrel embraced Enkidu. I'd probably place the Assamites as being from the actual line of Caine, since the concept of judges (although a lot different from the way we use the word today) is pretty big with the ancient Hebrews. Ventrue was probably a king from one of the earliest cities, perhaps Jericho. I've never completely nailed down a story for Brujah or Lasombra I completely liked, but Lasombra as Tiamat might work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T09:57:20-07:00","id":1408180,"title":"","content":"Some of the metaplot in v5 has issues with V20 rules (SI would be easier to deal with) and some are totally contrary (thinbloods alchemy replacing the thinblood's disciplines)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T10:24:05-07:00","id":1408184,"title":"","content":"Here is some of the head canon I am using for my current game. We are currently in 1999, using V20 rules. Once this current story arch is completed, we will do some down time wrap up of what the groups current characters are doing over the next 20 years, and then playing the same city, but in modern time using V5 rules.<br /> <br /> Blood pool -&gt; Hunger<br /> Various blood plagues over the years have change the interaction between vitae and human blood. The latest was caused by Baali during the Week of Nightmares, which is capped off by the solar Eclipse of September, 1999 ( which coincides with the battle of Ravnos)<br /> <br /> Tzimisce<br /> Using inspiration from the forums here, several koldunics including Dracula attempt to lessen the connection that Kupala has over their blood magic, and the corruptive influence he wields over Vissiccitude. As a result of the ritual they perform, non Path of Metamophosis vampires (and anything else) that were touched by Vissiccitude have that taint literally pour from their body, semi sentient. The blobs try and form together to recorrupt things around them. This begins an internal battle of wills for many Tzimisce, where the younger members of the clan begin to question and defy the still corrupted elders. The clan will eventually fracture, with the Tzimisce defecting from the Sabbat and the still corrupted Assuka remaining loyal.<br /> <br /> Tremere<br /> Another unintended consequence of the above ritual occurred in the Tremere. Because they had originally used Tzimisce blood in their rituals to make themselves vampires, they suffer greatly during the purge. Internal politics leads to infighting, with the added complication of the clan's blood so changed to deny the creation of blood bonds, allowing greater autonomy and free will among the clan.<br /> <br /> Ventrue<br /> Hardestadt is Ventrue, continuously reinventing himself in a younger generation. Always viewing himself a Shepard of humanity and the other clans, he created the Camarilla to do just that. Seeing the direction the sect was going, the rising human hunter movements, the Anarch movements and the rising Thin Bloods, he, approaches Jan Piertezoon and Theo Bell with a proposal. The current status quo is stagnating, and needs to be reinvigorated. Theo Bell will kill Hardestadt publically, galvanizing a figure the Anarchs can rally around and give the Anarch movement new life blood. The Camarilla will consolidate around the majority of the historic High Clans.<br /> <br /> Lasombra<br /> The founding clan see the strife and infighting of the Tzimisce, and begin to look inward for direction. Many take pilgrimages to the Abyss, some of them encountering a powerful, destructive entity. Some of the clan embrace the being, while other shun it, leading the the schism and defection of many Lasombra to the Camarilla<br /> <br /> Sabbat<br /> After the 4th civil war and the defections, those that carry the banner of the Sabbat are touched or corrupted in some way. These can be the Assuka, the Shalimite Lasombra, infiltrating Warrior Assamites with hidden loyalty to Ur-Shilgi or more openly infernal Baali and apoostates. The sect seems to have no unified goal, with those claiming to be Sabbat sometimes fighting amongst themselves more so than agaisnt the Camarilla or Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Church of Caine<br /> Those former Sabbat still cling to many of their ideals and notions, taking the Sword of Caine and redirecting it. Members of the Church instill themselves into both the Camarilla and the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu<br /> Not fully trusting the Inner Council when they demanded access to Schrekt.net, a dummy .net was created and handed over. Once it was seen that the Camarilla leadership was leaking selected information to the Second Inquisition to squash their opponents, the Nosferatu as a whole &quot;defect&quot; from everywhere. Publically, they remain a part of the Camarilla, retaining a seat on the inner council. Privately within the clan, it is even more so Clan above Sect. The assumed nature of the Niktuku as the servants of Absmiliard isn't quite qccurate. Absmiliard hates all of his children equally. The Niktuku are those Nosferatu that keep other Nosferatu from attracting his attention. They will seek out an destroy Nosferatu that become too famous or garner too much attention.<br /> <br /> Ravnos<br /> The master of illusions, performed the greatest slight of hand and distraction. Drawing the attention of the Technocracy and the spirit nuke, they are attempting to realize their goal of transcendance by becoming a yama king by using the irradiated chi created in the nukes wake. The remnants of the clan redouble their efforts of hunting and erradiating demons and Keui Jin.<br /> <br /> Gehenna<br /> It is during one of the cyclical Gehennas, the one of 1999, that many other changes occur. it is in the aftermath that you see the rise of the Thin Bloods, along with the more mutability of the blood and vampiric powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T11:52:28-07:00","id":1408202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408006-v20-5-best-of-both-headcanon-thread?p=1408180#post1408180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the metaplot in v5 has issues with V20 rules (SI would be easier to deal with) and some are totally contrary (thinbloods alchemy replacing the thinblood's disciplines)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya, you'd have to adapt the thin blood alchemy a bit, if you wanted to. Or you could stick with the existing V20/revised rules and let them create their own low level disciplines like before, they're thematically similar enough. Another possibility is using the anarch sorcery from the V20 Rites of Blood. There's not really that much at all that needs much reworking to dump the metaplot in, though and it'd be easy enough to just use the existing systems from earlier or dump the thin blood alchemy right in and allow them to mimic powers, they just require a blood point instead of a rouse check. There's plenty of easy ways to do it without much work at all. It just depends on how you like your thin bloods and there's lots of options.<br /> <br /> I don't really see it as necessarily being that much easier to deal with the SI when you combine it with the beckoning and most of the elders taking off, especially since the SI would try to strike during the day. In my mind, the Technocracy is the hand behind the Second Inquisition. So they've got some real power behind them. It doesn't require any toning down of vampire powers to make them a threat. Even without Technocracy agents being directly involved in a raid, you've still got heavily armed mortals going after vampires when they're at their weakest. A highly trained military group with advanced weaponry and surveillance equipment would easily be a match for most vampires during the day. Also Vienna was an inside job with either Tremere or Saulot blinding the clan to the attack.<br /> <br /> I do honestly feel like the SI was a bit of a heavy handed approach to dealing with the problem that there were just too damned many elders and ancients in every major city and it kind of breaks the theme of the hoary old vampires manipulating everything from behind the scenes. Who knows, maybe there are some hands of Methuselahs or Antedeluvians involved in it? I think the Beckoning would have been enough and it changes the theme from being manipulative movers and shakers from behind the scenes to being hunted too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T13:13:31-07:00","id":1408228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408006-v20-5-best-of-both-headcanon-thread?p=1408061#post1408061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own personal take has been that any connection between Set (or rather, the vampire cult that worships him) and Apep/Apophis is entirely that of werewolves trying to fit parts of human mythology into their own cosmology (much in the way they consider Fenris a hero and Odin and the other Aesir villains).<br /> <br /> The Set of Vampire, meanwhile, is/was the Lord of the Red Desert, a creature of unrestrained aggression and instinct, a living storm who stands in stark contrast to his much more balanced and restrained brother Osiris, the Lord of the Black Soil, and the other god-like Antediluvian (in the pre-Flood sense, not the ancient vampire sense) beings of Heliopolis. He is loyal to Ra (the Sun) and fights for him, but at some point, he turns against his brother and murders him. At this point, he's an outcast and at war with the rest of his family, and it's during this time that he becomes a vampire. (Again, this is my own personal take.) If you're a Noddist, this is when he meets Cain(e) (I ignore the second generation), but parts of his Set's cult believe that he became a vampire on his own, either doing something in the underworld or as a result of killing his brother. But at this point, he's fully a creature of Isfet, the counterpart to Ma'at (and neither concept/force can exist without the other).</div> </div> </div> </div>There are many different ways an ST can handle Set. That's because the game uses several different inspirations for this antedeluvian, and every ST will latch onto different elements.<ul><li>We have the general story of the unique WoD mythology that applies to every antedeluvian.</li> <li>We have the layer of Egyptian mythology known to popular culture.</li> <li>We have the specific euhemeristic interpretation of this in VtM. For those unfamiliar with the term euhemerism is an interpretation of mythology that is the mythological personages and events are based on real people and events. One thing I liked about early WoD is that A lot (but not all) of mythological accounts are euhemeristic. It gives me a lot to play with as ST.</li> <li>More informed people also know that Egyptian mythology, like all mythologies, changed over time (and place!) bringing forth new ideas, new gods, new stories, and the religious officials constantly updating, reconciling, and transforming these stories to make sense to them at this time.</li> <li>We have the Robert E. Howard use of Set as the name for the &quot;Great Serpent&quot; of evil that is found throughout many of his tales.</li> </ul>Combined, these are extremely contradictory and incoherent. So any ST concerned with this will need to choose what elements he prefers and emphasizes. Personally, I love the use of Howardiana in the World of Darkness, but it is obvious many people don't understand its place in the game (if they are not familiar with the works of Howard, it goes over their heads), and some who do know it don't like it.<br /> <br /> So I like to preserve the Followers of Set as a cult of Wyrm worshippers. They have a very specific dogma and goals as such. That specific dogma and their success as a clan sets them apart from Sabbat (and other vampire) infernalists and the Baali. They have a very similar understanding of the Triat (which these other groups don't) as the Garou, but within their own mythology (this is one reason why the Setites and Black Spiral Dancers aren't allies; they consider the other to be heretics). <br /> <br /> (I think the clan works less well as a Vampire specific element, but works extremely well as a World of Darkness element that helps tie the game to others. When I first played, I didn't care for this so I minimized the Setites role in my games. But since I now like a more integrated setting (while avoiding a Monster Mash style) I find a lot more use for them. It also helps explain why they are an Independent clan - they're so busy with non-vampire stuff, they actually don't want to deal with the diversion of vampire politics.)<br /> <br /> In my chronicles, the Setite antedeluvian was a high priest of the Wyrm before the Flood. Let's call him Typhon to distinguish him from the Wyrm (aka Apophis) and Set (the Egyptian personage). Set, Osiris, Isis, and many of the other Egyptian pantheon were real historical personages post flood, somewhere around 5000-4000 BC. Typhon embraces Set, making him of the 4th generation. Typhon also embraced other 4th generation childer in other lands, but only Set survived long term (Set's childer are the dominant lineage, but a few vampires descended from other destroyed lines did survive - these often cause problems within the clan because their teachings don't mirror the dominant Egyptian strand). When Typhon eventually went into torpor, Set &quot;pulled a Hardestadt&quot; and essentially took his place, and gradually it was his name that was assigned to the antedeluvian. Most of the historical accounts of Set are actually of this 4th generation vampire, not Typhon.<br /> <br /> Typhon eventually left Egypt moving south down the Nile, leaving Set &quot;in charge&quot; of what would become the dominant block of his descendants. Set was eventually forced out of Egypt by Horus, the Cult of Isis, and Silent Striders (among others). Things went well for a long time, and the common people just remembered the good stories about Set (before he was embraced). Then Set returned to Egypt during the Hyksos Invasion and began purging the land of his enemies. This is when Set's image in popular Egyptian imagination changed, and he became outright evil.<br /> <br /> [I've never made up my mind though about who embraced Osiris. While many feel he too was embraced in the same clan as Set, I prefer to think of him as one of Cappadocius's childer. Osiris is a Greek variant of Ashur which is one of Cappadocius's possible names, and Osiris' eventual role as a lord of the dead fits within the Cappadocian theme. I also like the idea that this means the Children of Osiris (which is an extremely small sect in my game, not a &quot;bloodline&quot;) became the home of some of the more humane Cappadocians escaping the Giovanni purge.]<br /> <br /> Noddists have a hard time figuring out stuff about Set because he's not the actual antedeluvian, but this isn't clear to anyone outside an extremely small circle of the Setite clan. So Noddists come up with things like the Set-Osiris myth is just a misinterpretation of the Cain-Abel myth.<br /> <br /> I run the clan according to strict gnostic-style cult lines. Clan/religious secrets are only revealed to trusted individuals who advance to the next level. Much teaching requires esoteric knowledge because everything is not what it seems. The clan controls many different occult, religious, or philosophical front organizations that recruit and teach normal humans that begin the process of indoctrination. Eventually some of these people advance to the next level and become aware of vampires and taught Set-specific teachings. They become retainers to actual vampires (some become ghouls, but not all). And the clan only embraces a select culling of these people in order to ensure their loyalty to the greater clan/cult organization. (This greatly changes how people become Setite vampires. The clanbooks assume the Setites embrace like the other clans, grabbing suitable people off the streets, instead of operating in an actual cult like manner of indoctrinating people first.)<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's not for everyone, but it works for me.<br /> <br /> However, because of this (and other head canon), it really prevents me from using any of the V5 major setting element changes except as a matter of broad inspiration.<br /> <br /> My preference would be for the game to stop trying to pretend there is one inherent canon anymore. Every edition changes discards many elements introduced in prior editions, and only keeps what it wants. It needs to understand many players and STs do the same. It would be better to adopt a toolkit approach and give these metaplot elements only as ideas an ST could use in their game, and to state there are multiple versions of the WoD - the early Andrew Greenberg version, the late second edition version, the Revised era of Sabbat Crusades, and this new V5 version. Clarify how they are different, and how each makes for a different game. Make it clear ALL are appropriate versions, and that STs can create their own version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408006-v20-5-best-of-both-headcanon-thread?p=1408137#post1408137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems less interesting, then a story of a God that was Demonized because of his Association With foreigners and thus foreign Conquers, to be more interesting then White Wolfs crappy version,</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone has different tastes.<br /> <br /> Some people really want to use the real world mythology to define the clan. I remember there was once an excellent World of Darkness/Vampire website online by a Frenchmen who was really into Egyptian mythology and he worked out how to reconcile salient WoD canon while keeping to mythology and its historical changes. He did everything he could to purge the Howardian elements, or at least reveal that as a later corruption. It was very impressive. Ultimately not to my taste, but I wouldn't complain about it if I ever played in his game. Individual STs can make their own decisions about this.<br /> <br /> Others really like the Revised tribebook interpretation. Which I think has some good elements to it, but in my opinion totally changed what the clan was about.<br /> <br /> Some like to imagine that Set killing Osiris is simply another version of Cain killing Abel, and interpret everything in an uncomplicated Noddist mythology with only fiddly bits of actual Egyptian mythology and/or Howardian elements.<br /> <br /> None of that is wrong or right. De gustibus non est disputandum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T15:45:26-07:00","id":1408266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408006-v20-5-best-of-both-headcanon-thread?p=1408228#post1408228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone has different tastes.<br /> <br /> Some people really want to use the real world mythology to define the clan. I remember there was once an excellent World of Darkness/Vampire website online by a Frenchmen who was really into Egyptian mythology and he worked out how to reconcile salient WoD canon while keeping to mythology and its historical changes. He did everything he could to purge the Howardian elements, or at least reveal that as a later corruption. It was very impressive. Ultimately not to my taste, but I wouldn't complain about it if I ever played in his game. Individual STs can make their own decisions about this.<br /> <br /> Others really like the Revised tribebook interpretation. Which I think has some good elements to it, but in my opinion totally changed what the clan was about.<br /> <br /> Some like to imagine that Set killing Osiris is simply another version of Cain killing Abel, and interpret everything in an uncomplicated Noddist mythology with only fiddly bits of actual Egyptian mythology and/or Howardian elements.<br /> <br /> None of that is wrong or right. De gustibus non est disputandum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Similarly, I know a guy who cannot stand Assassins Creed. I mean, he has a kind of insane aversion to the game series that comes from something being REALLY personal to him. He hates:<br /> <br /> * Ancient Aliens<br /> * Conspiracy theories<br /> * Illuminati groups<br /> * Secret Histories<br /> * Genetic memory<br /> <br /> Here's the thing, he LOVES history, though. Loves it so much that seeing all of these essential elements in an otherwise incredible reproduction of history makes him violently ill. He desperately just wants an AC series without anything resembling AC.<br /> <br /> I'm like, &quot;I don't see it as a history series. I see it as a fantasy series with history elements.&quot;<br /> <br /> And he just gets pissed at me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T18:16:35-07:00","id":1408297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408006-v20-5-best-of-both-headcanon-thread?p=1408057#post1408057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's fine, I've asked several questions related to Lucita in media and often make fun of myself regarding being her fanboy.<br /> <br /> Hilariously, Dixie from Onyx Path had the same bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aight, sounds good - just wanted to make sure everything was kosher in that regard. Sorry about making a thing of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T18:36:04-07:00","id":1408300,"title":"","content":"<b>The Withering and Beckoning</b><br /> <br /> * I actually did this in my V5 game.<br /> <br /> Why is the Kindred nation falling apart?<br /> <br /> For millennia, the Elders of the Camarilla and Sabbat have been able to keep control over the Anarchs due to the simple raw power they wielded both through their Disciplines as well as their vast network of agents. The invention of automatic firearms helped even things out in a few places (mostly places where such were readily available) but even that could not make it so a 6th generation Prince was vulnerable to a 13th generation one.<br /> <br /> This has all changed in the past ten years as the power of Elders and even Methuselahs have dramatically weakened. Elders who could once reach across continents to control their progeny find themselves reduced to having the same level of power as a dedicated Ancilla. Even centuries old vampires close to Caine find themselves with no more strength than those of the 8th or 9th generation.<br /> <br /> The Withering is the worst sign of Gehenna for Elders as it means that even those who felt they would be powerful and able to resist the ancients are stripped of anything that makes them invulnerable. It also effects their networks of power as well with Ventrue, Lasombra, and Tremere networks collapsing in on themselves. People dominated for decades or even centuries suddenly snap out of their control to lash at their former masters.<br /> <br /> The Withering has been kept a secret from all but the oldest of the Camarilla as it is barely noticeable for American Elders and those embraced in the past two centuries. It has, however, had consequences that are becoming apparent in their magnitude. Anarch revolts that would have been put down easily just a decade prior have succeeded. Ancient vampires over a thousand years old have fallen prey to the fangs of their distant rivals. The Thin Bloods have managed to form into a faction versus being stomped out wherever they emerge.<br /> <br /> Some have suggested that there is a cure for this condition and it requires venturing to the Middle East in order to answer a distant call of an ancient power. Those who believe in Gehenna believe they will be judged by the Antediluvians and either devoured or restored to their full power. Others believe this so-called &quot;Beckoning&quot; and perhaps the Withering as well is just the work of the Assamite Ur-Shulgi, wielding his near limitless might and call for the US military to bomb Alamut into the ground.<br /> <br /> Others turn to folk remedies like diablerie of Kindred or the feeding of Thin Bloods in order to sustain their powers. It is known that both can potentially ward off the Withering's worst effects but the costs for one's humanity are considerable. Once humane Kindred have degenerated to becoming rampaging cannibalistic beasts, which only continues the spiral of irrelevancy. Once vast alien geniuses are becoming no smarter or cunning than the smartest human--and that might as well be the smartest termite when trying to out-think the ancients.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T11:10:21-07:00","id":1408515,"title":"","content":"Sorry about the quiet here folks, I\u2019ve been off the forums with dome hectic irl stuff, but I\u2019m back rn so lemme get out some responses.<br /> <br /> As for the Set &amp; everyone\u2019s fave Egyptian Darkness Serpent, it comes back as so much does for me to Multi-Resonance Layered Reality. We have Set &amp; Osiris as vampires, primordial Mages, Gaian spirits, firstborn fae, higher umbra spirits, lower umbra spirits, as well as quite potentially both literal demons and literal gods. Which for me, I can square the circle of making that work for my purposes in running WoD, but I also totally understand why others may prefer other routes.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve actually been working on some ideas regarding Vienna and the Tremere Schism as well which I\u2019m gonna work at gathering my thoughts on and post a bit later I think.<br /> <br /> Using rituals to adapt blood pool to hunger is interesting SarcasticJazzyhands, I don\u2019t think that\u2019s something I would have thought of! You\u2019ve got a lot of really interesting ideas and I don\u2019t think I can reply to each of them right now, they do feel like really interesting ways to go about things.<br /> <br /> <br /> That\u2019s also a really interesting take Black Fox, I\u2019ll need to give that some thought myself about how I handle Set.<br /> <br /> The Withering &amp; Beckoning is one of the elements of V5 that I\u2019m the most torn about because I do appreciate its ability to clean the slate in many cases where I feel WW went overboard with the elders and methuselahs, but it\u2019s also a balancing act for me because I don\u2019t want to use it to shake up the setting super hard, just polish off some rough edges and perhaps add a twist which plots can be built upon as a mysterious call to the places of the ancients. It\u2019s one of the ones I\u2019m still thinking about a great deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T13:31:56-07:00","id":1408565,"title":"","content":"There's a withering in V5? <br /> <br /> Regarding the beckoning... that's one of the things of V5 that's really... a neonate perspective, not what's actually going on. Nobody's being beckoned, that's just an excuse to explain the mass hiding of elders for political reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T13:36:01-07:00","id":1408566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408006-v20-5-best-of-both-headcanon-thread?p=1408565#post1408565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a withering in V5?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> Hence why it's in a V20 thread.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T19:42:50-07:00","id":1408636,"title":"","content":"Very interesting post, Black Fox.<br /> <br /> In a sense, it's not so much Vampire:the Masquerade itself creating problems with Set, it's the other lines, because they tend to be much more clear-cut. The Setites' clanbook was much more open to interpretation compared to Mummy's telling of events.<br /> <br /> Heck, for all we know, the Followers' Antediluvian is a serpent-shifting ginger from Greece named Typhon, who wandered into Egypt once and then the local priests, mages, and Fera began identifying him with the local god of foreigners, Set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T08:12:32-07:00","id":1409563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SarcasticJazzHands</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408006-v20-5-best-of-both-headcanon-thread?p=1408184#post1408184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is some of the head canon I am using for my current game. We are currently in 1999, using V20 rules. Once this current story arch is completed, we will do some down time wrap up of what the groups current characters are doing over the next 20 years, and then playing the same city, but in modern time using V5 rules.<br /> <br /> Blood pool -&gt; Hunger<br /> Various blood plagues over the years have change the interaction between vitae and human blood. The latest was caused by Baali during the Week of Nightmares, which is capped off by the solar Eclipse of September, 1999 ( which coincides with the battle of Ravnos)<br /> <br /> Tzimisce<br /> Using inspiration from the forums here, several koldunics including Dracula attempt to lessen the connection that Kupala has over their blood magic, and the corruptive influence he wields over Vissiccitude. As a result of the ritual they perform, non Path of Metamophosis vampires (and anything else) that were touched by Vissiccitude have that taint literally pour from their body, semi sentient. The blobs try and form together to recorrupt things around them. This begins an internal battle of wills for many Tzimisce, where the younger members of the clan begin to question and defy the still corrupted elders. The clan will eventually fracture, with the Tzimisce defecting from the Sabbat and the still corrupted Assuka remaining loyal.<br /> <br /> Tremere<br /> Another unintended consequence of the above ritual occurred in the Tremere. Because they had originally used Tzimisce blood in their rituals to make themselves vampires, they suffer greatly during the purge. Internal politics leads to infighting, with the added complication of the clan's blood so changed to deny the creation of blood bonds, allowing greater autonomy and free will among the clan.<br /> <br /> Ventrue<br /> Hardestadt is Ventrue, continuously reinventing himself in a younger generation. Always viewing himself a Shepard of humanity and the other clans, he created the Camarilla to do just that. Seeing the direction the sect was going, the rising human hunter movements, the Anarch movements and the rising Thin Bloods, he, approaches Jan Piertezoon and Theo Bell with a proposal. The current status quo is stagnating, and needs to be reinvigorated. Theo Bell will kill Hardestadt publically, galvanizing a figure the Anarchs can rally around and give the Anarch movement new life blood. The Camarilla will consolidate around the majority of the historic High Clans.<br /> <br /> Lasombra<br /> The founding clan see the strife and infighting of the Tzimisce, and begin to look inward for direction. Many take pilgrimages to the Abyss, some of them encountering a powerful, destructive entity. Some of the clan embrace the being, while other shun it, leading the the schism and defection of many Lasombra to the Camarilla<br /> <br /> Sabbat<br /> After the 4th civil war and the defections, those that carry the banner of the Sabbat are touched or corrupted in some way. These can be the Assuka, the Shalimite Lasombra, infiltrating Warrior Assamites with hidden loyalty to Ur-Shilgi or more openly infernal Baali and apoostates. The sect seems to have no unified goal, with those claiming to be Sabbat sometimes fighting amongst themselves more so than agaisnt the Camarilla or Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Church of Caine<br /> Those former Sabbat still cling to many of their ideals and notions, taking the Sword of Caine and redirecting it. Members of the Church instill themselves into both the Camarilla and the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu<br /> Not fully trusting the Inner Council when they demanded access to Schrekt.net, a dummy .net was created and handed over. Once it was seen that the Camarilla leadership was leaking selected information to the Second Inquisition to squash their opponents, the Nosferatu as a whole &amp;quot;defect&amp;quot; from everywhere. Publically, they remain a part of the Camarilla, retaining a seat on the inner council. Privately within the clan, it is even more so Clan above Sect. The assumed nature of the Niktuku as the servants of Absmiliard isn't quite qccurate. Absmiliard hates all of his children equally. The Niktuku are those Nosferatu that keep other Nosferatu from attracting his attention. They will seek out an destroy Nosferatu that become too famous or garner too much attention.<br /> <br /> Ravnos<br /> The master of illusions, performed the greatest slight of hand and distraction. Drawing the attention of the Technocracy and the spirit nuke, they are attempting to realize their goal of transcendance by becoming a yama king by using the irradiated chi created in the nukes wake. The remnants of the clan redouble their efforts of hunting and erradiating demons and Keui Jin.<br /> <br /> Gehenna<br /> It is during one of the cyclical Gehennas, the one of 1999, that many other changes occur. it is in the aftermath that you see the rise of the Thin Bloods, along with the more mutability of the blood and vampiric powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait what did V5 do to the Blood pool/hunger Thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}